# Copy this file to .env and replace placeholders.
# Never commit .env.
#
# How this file is read (edgeconnect-auto, src/edgeconnect_automation/config.py):
# - ./.env in the current folder, or the file given with --dotenv <path>. Parent and
#   home folders are never searched.
# - One KEY=value per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are skipped, and a
#   leading "export " is allowed. A value may be wrapped in matching '...' or "...".
#   There are no inline comments: everything after = is the value, so keep notes on
#   their own lines. A line without = stops the run with "invalid dotenv line <N>".
# - An empty value counts as not set.
# - Process environment variables override this file (same key names, any case for
#   orch_<N> and <nickname>_* keys).
# - This CLI reads no on/off switches and no numbers from .env. Timeouts and retries
#   are fixed in code: 30 s per HTTP request, 3 attempts for GET reads, 120 s to
#   verify a change, 5 s between verification polls. Plain http:// is possible only
#   with the --allow-http command option, and only for localhost / 127.x / ::1.
#
# setup.sh writes one shared .env used by edgeconnect-auto, edgeconnect-preconfig and
# the edgeconnect-mcp server. This CLI ignores the keys of the other two, such as
# EC_VALIDATORS and <nickname>_mcp_*; they are documented in those repos' .env.example.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One Orchestrator
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Orchestrator address. Required (here, or per nickname below).
# Accepted: https://<host>[:<port>] with an empty path or /gms/rest (a trailing / is
#   fine); the host can be a name or an IP. No user:password@, ?query or #fragment.
# Bad value: stops with "base URL must be an absolute HTTPS URL",
#   "base URL path must be empty or /gms/rest" or
#   "base URL must not include credentials, query, or fragment".
# Aliases, first one set wins: orchestrator_base_url, ORCHESTRATOR_BASE_URL,
#   EDGECONNECT_BASE_URL, EC_BASE_URL (process environment first, then this file).
# Examples: https://orchestrator.example.com  https://192.0.2.10:8443/gms/rest
orchestrator_base_url=https://orchestrator.example.com

# Orchestrator REST API key, sent in the header named by orchestrator_api_key_header.
# Required. Any text; not checked until Orchestrator answers (a wrong key gives HTTP 401/403).
# Missing: stops with "Orchestrator base URL and API key are required ...".
# Aliases: orchestrator_api_key, ORCHESTRATOR_API_KEY, EDGECONNECT_API_KEY, EC_API_KEY.
orchestrator_api_key=<API_KEY>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TLS and authentication (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Private CA bundle used to verify the Orchestrator certificate.
# Default: the system trust store, with the host name checked.
# Accepted: path to an existing PEM file (absolute path recommended; a relative path is
#   taken from the current folder).
# Bad value: stops with "CA bundle does not exist".
# Aliases: orchestrator_ca_bundle, ORCHESTRATOR_CA_BUNDLE, EDGECONNECT_CA_BUNDLE,
#   REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE, SSL_CERT_FILE. The last two are often already set in a shell
#   by other tools and are picked up too.
# Also the default for every nickname that has no <nickname>_ca_bundle.
# orchestrator_ca_bundle=/absolute/path/to/ca-bundle.pem

# Name of the HTTP header that carries the API key.
# Default: X-Auth-Token. Set it only when Orchestrator expects another header.
# Accepted: an HTTP header name (no colon or line break). Not checked when loading:
#   a name with a colon fails at the first request with "Invalid header name"; a
#   valid but wrong name gives HTTP 401/403.
# Aliases: orchestrator_api_key_header, ORCHESTRATOR_API_KEY_HEADER,
#   EDGECONNECT_API_KEY_HEADER.
# Also the default for every nickname that has no <nickname>_api_key_header.
# orchestrator_api_key_header=X-Auth-Token

# Pin a self-signed certificate by its SHA-256 fingerprint. When set, the CA bundle
#   and host-name checks are replaced by an exact match of the server certificate on
#   every connection; a mismatch fails every request (reported as a transport failure).
# Default: not pinned.
# Accepted: 64 hex digits, upper or lower case, colons allowed
#   (AB:CD:... as printed by "openssl x509 -noout -fingerprint -sha256").
# Bad value: stops with "TLS certificate pin must be a SHA-256 fingerprint
#   (64 hex digits, colons allowed)".
# Aliases: orchestrator_tls_sha256, ORCHESTRATOR_TLS_SHA256.
# Per host only: it pins this single-Orchestrator address (also when it appears as the
#   "orchestrator" choice next to nicknames) and is never a default for nicknames.
# orchestrator_tls_sha256=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Several Orchestrators, chosen by nickname
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The nickname is what you type on the command line:
#   edgeconnect-auto --orchestrator lab discovery
# If orchestrator_base_url and orchestrator_api_key are also set, they become one more
# choice with the nickname "orchestrator".

# orch_<N>=<nickname> registers an Orchestrator. N is a whole number; the numbers set
#   the menu order and need not be consecutive. An empty value is skipped.
# Nickname: letters, digits and _ ([a-z0-9_]+ after lower-casing, so Prod = prod).
#   Not allowed: default, orchestrator, edgeconnect, ec. Do not use "orch" or a nickname
#   starting with "orch_": its keys (orch_base_url) are read as bad slots and stop the run.
# Bad value: a non-numbered slot (orch_prod=...) stops with "Orchestrator slots must be
#   numbered"; a bad or reserved nickname stops with "an Orchestrator nickname must use
#   letters, digits or _ ..."; the same nickname twice stops with "... is used by both".
# orch_1=prod
# orch_2=lab

# Per nickname, required: <nickname>_base_url and <nickname>_api_key, with the same
#   accepted values as orchestrator_base_url and orchestrator_api_key.
# Missing either: stops with "Orchestrator '<nickname>' (orch_<N>) needs both
#   <nickname>_base_url and <nickname>_api_key" when that nickname is chosen.
# prod_base_url=https://orchestrator.example.com
# prod_api_key=<API_KEY>
# lab_base_url=https://192.0.2.20
# lab_api_key=<API_KEY>

# Per nickname, optional: same accepted values as the orchestrator_* keys above.
# <nickname>_ca_bundle      default: orchestrator_ca_bundle (or its aliases), else system trust store
# <nickname>_api_key_header default: orchestrator_api_key_header (or its aliases), else X-Auth-Token
# <nickname>_tls_sha256     default: not pinned. orchestrator_tls_sha256 is NOT used for
#                           nicknames: a pin belongs to one host, so pin each nickname itself.
# prod_ca_bundle=/absolute/path/to/ca-bundle.pem
# prod_api_key_header=X-Auth-Token
# lab_tls_sha256=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef

# Orchestrator used when --orchestrator is not given (--orchestrator always wins).
# Accepted: a nickname (prod), a slot (orch_1), or "orchestrator" for the
#   single-Orchestrator lines; any case.
# Default: the only Orchestrator if just one is configured; otherwise a numbered menu
#   in a terminal, and in a script the run stops with "multiple Orchestrators are
#   configured (...); choose one with --orchestrator NAME or set orch_default in .env".
# Bad value: stops with "unknown Orchestrator '<name>'; configured: ...".
# Ignored when no orch_<N> lines exist.
# orch_default=prod

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reports (process environment only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# EDGECONNECT_REPORT_DIR is read from the process environment only, NOT from this file.
# Folder for the automatic per-workflow report log (<workflow>.log and .jsonl).
# Default: ./reports in the current folder. --report-dir <folder> overrides it.
# Accepted: any folder path (created when needed); an empty value disables the log.
# Example (shell): export EDGECONNECT_REPORT_DIR=/var/tmp/ec-reports
